# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# The reader's gzipped corpus start-up cache, written beside data/kjv.jsonl
# when the repo itself is the data home. Regenerated; never commit.
*.idxcache

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Don't ship any documentation we map to JSON
*.docx
*.doc
*.pdf

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# .NET build output (from the C# binding demo)
**/bin/
**/obj/
# …but NOT Rust's src/bin/ crate-binary sources (e.g. the plumbline-bindgen tool),
# which the broad **/bin/ rule above would otherwise swallow.
!**/src/bin/
!**/src/bin/**

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Personal study data written when the repo root is the data home (dev/testing);
# never commit — the reader's own tags/weaves/threads/notes. This list is the
# web home's USER_DIRS (apps/web/src/engine/home.ts) plus weaves/suggested and
# the retired patches dir; three of them were missing until 2026-07-29, which is
# the same hole that let 224 stock files sit tracked against this file's intent.
# The CI step "nothing is tracked against .gitignore" is the guard.
/tags/
/weaves/
/threads/
/notes/
/memory/
/reading/
/suggested/
/.config/
# The Ed25519 point-patch/rule layer was never ported (see CLAUDE.md's
# architecture table); a patches/ dir at the root is dev leftovers, not data.
/patches/

# Web shell (apps/web) build artifacts — regenerated by npm run pack:data / pack:wasm / build
apps/web/node_modules/
apps/web/dist/
apps/web/public/pack/
apps/web/public/plumbline_ffi.wasm

# Generated on demand by scripts/hymnal-review.mjs for a read-through of the
# hymn texts and charts. Not a source file and not worth versioning: it is one
# command away whenever it is wanted.
HYMNAL-REVIEW.md
__pycache__/

# The Han face's 24 MB upstream source — fetched (sha256-pinned) by
# apps/web/scripts/subset-fonts.mjs, never committed; only the built
# public/fonts/*.woff2 ships. The other fonts-src TTFs are small and stay.
apps/web/fonts-src/NotoSerifCJKtc-Regular.otf
